Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P5.5 stage sweep hook in updateModeTask (DW3_CHEATS builds only)

Opt-in test run (stage_sweep=1 in port_options.cfg, docs/P5.5_STAGE_SWEEP.md):
once per game frame of the mode task, dw3_sweep_tick() gets the game mode and
names the mode to request next (STAGSLCT -> stage -> STAGSLCT -> ...). The
party is seeded first, as the P3.8 sweep aids (patch 0030) do. The tick is a
no-op unless the key is set. The debug stage select's TASK_KILL does not
overwrite the requested mode while the sweep is on (the env check of patch
0030 has no equivalent on the Switch). Every line is inside #ifdef DW3_CHEATS.

--- a/src/engine/system/overlay.c
+++ b/src/engine/system/overlay.c
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@
 char *getenv(const char *name);
 long strtol(const char *nptr, char **endptr, int base);
 void exit(int status);
+#ifdef DW3_CHEATS
+#include "port_stage_sweep.h"
+#endif
 /* Armed by CARDGAME return when DW3_AFTER_CARD_ALBUM is set. */
 s32 DW3_afterCardAlbumArm;
 #endif
@@ -223,6 +226,20 @@
             }
         }
 #endif
+#ifdef DW3_CHEATS
+        /* P5.5 stage sweep (opt-in: stage_sweep=1 in port_options.cfg): one
+           call per game frame; the sweep names the mode to request next */
+        if (dw3_sweep_enabled()) {
+            s32 sweepMode = dw3_sweep_tick((int)GAME.funcs.getMode());
+
+            if (sweepMode != 0) {
+                if (GAME.funcs.getPartyMember(0) < 0) {
+                    GAME.funcs.setParty(0);
+                }
+                GAME.funcs.requestMode(sweepMode, 0);
+            }
+        }
+#endif
         if (GAME.funcs.isModeChangePending() != 0) {
             task->setState(task, TASK_KILL);
         }
